  "problems": [
    "extra-large-dog-beds: Shopify rejects CONTAINS conditions under 3 characters (after trimming), so ia.json rules VARIANT_TITLE CONTAINS \"XL\" and TITLE CONTAINS \"XL\" were rejected. Replaced with equivalent rules: VARIANT_TITLE STARTS_WITH \"XL\", VARIANT_TITLE CONTAINS \"/ XL\", VARIANT_TITLE CONTAINS \"XXL\", TITLE CONTAINS \"XXL\", TITLE CONTAINS \"XL Orthopaedic\" (+ original Extra Large and xl dog bed tag rules). Matches the same 27 products in the catalogue snapshot; a future product with a bare \" XL \" in its title only (no XL variant) needs the tag \"xl dog bed\".",
    "memory-foam-dog-beds shows 19 products (expected 18) because of a product titled \"Ww\" (gid://shopify/Product/11338056761686, handle ww, GBP 5.00, ACTIVE, no type/tags, no images, created 2026-10-03T02:27Z) that is published to the Online Store, live at /products/ww and listed in this collection. It looks like a stray test product; it was not touched (products were out of scope apart from image alts). Archive/delete it or set it to draft.",
    "The intro text was saved to the custom.intro metafield (multi_line_text_field) on all 18 collections, but the live theme does not read it: its collection hero shows the first sentences of the collection description, as theme/sections/collection-hero.liquid does. To show the intro, the hero needs a theme change (e.g. use collection.metafields.custom.intro.value before falling back to the description). No theme files were changed.",
    "The 4 new menus exist but are not shown yet. The live theme still points at main-menu and footer, which were left unchanged as instructed. Select lunova-main-menu and the lunova-footer-* menus in the theme editor header/footer settings to use them.",
    "The existing contact page title stays \"Contact\"; pages/contact.json has \"Contact Us\". Only the body and SEO were updated, as instructed.",
    "Smart-collection rules were otherwise applied exactly as in ia.json (column/relation names already matched the CollectionRuleColumn/CollectionRuleRelation enums)."
  ]
